p4AgE&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQQjacZ0kDicnb6TR9rKXwiRUnNSxRCsjAl8FPQNMTUINw&oe=6AFDC00A"}, {"file_name": "02_flame.png", "id": "1141418878434135", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/604385997_1141418881767468_8658686861929585272_n.png?_nc_cat=107&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=ccJLtXQAfuIQ7kNvwHeYbt9&_nc_oc=Adr_eaELEnQvMXtz8fbch-QQ0NXtp51Drkhqg1rm34FjFyDaTrW3n6xeSp4-p05cFqY&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQQ8dZLs_tEhI6j5B39ASKCJDTEhPpsuC1MhyrRrFus-Vg&oe=6AFDCB25"}, {"file_name": "05_melting.png", "id": "1173310015258700", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/596068480_1173310018592033_6702046555256473668_n.png?_nc_cat=108&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=tEX5fWbeepsQ7kNvwE2Q1HZ&_nc_oc=Adq8StGPgzHaO7s0GTqGS-Op_S8P0uwi13sSCIbsNJM1UEjkpoc4a-V_OCA9oYX5CcI&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQRkolpFMVLayoXHUmVtzogLC9jGwQAZWa7-4kQSJA-AoA&oe=6AFDCBF2"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "cover_landscape_2560x1440.png", "id": "2127414711213681", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/795000614_2127414714547014_4499025661318232458_n.png?_nc_cat=110&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=RHUnpSow-HQQ7kNvwGOF2ZJ&_nc_oc=AdpcNAkpOR8r9HXqo0-yoaQr9Q4g4ac_ysF2stg0oF0lpiO_tFdB3EE3mcFV93Bn-FU&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQS-isDqR92ZYGhS2WwQhxKfac5E737pr9XIMvbn_04hIw&oe=6AFDE36D"}, "display_name": "BeakerWise: The Real Science Lab", "keywords": [], "long_description": "A LAB ON YOUR TABLE\nIn mixed reality a virtual lab bench sits on your real table. Or work in a virtual science room. Burettes, Bunsen burners, circuits, lenses and microscopes, all virtual. Play seated. Every action also has a button on the panel.\n\n104 EXPERIMENTS\n21 in biology, 28 in chemistry, 33 in physics and 22 simpler first experiments. From melting ice and magnets to titrations, flame colours and light through two slits. Many are linked to the practical skills in the Department for Education's GCSE and A level science subject content for England.\n\nREAL DATA, HONEST LABELS\nMost results are calculated from real data, such as NIST and IAPWS values. A label always says what you see. When a number is a good guess, the app says so. The \"How we know\" card names the sources.\n\nSAFETY FIRST\nA safety card before every experiment says if it is safe at home, needs an adult, or is for a school lab or a teacher only. The app shows good habits, such as goggles before a flame. It helps you prepare for a practical. It does not replace doing it in a school lab.\n\nCLEAR FOR EVERYONE\nFour reading depths, from Quick Look to Expert. A computer-generated British voice reads aloud, with subtitles. Magnifiers for fine readings, and results in tables and graphs.\n\nFOR FAMILIES\nUp to six explorers, pictures only, no names. Break reminders. An adult should supervise children's play. No ads, no chat, no accounts, no in-app purchases and no personal data collected. Plays offline.", "short_description": "Science practicals on a virtual lab bench. In mixed reality the bench sits on your real table, or work in a virtual science room. 104 experiments in biology, chemistry and physics, from melting ice to titrations and flame colours. Most results are calculated from real, sourced data, and the app says when a number is a good guess. Four reading depths, from short and simple to expert detail. For ages 10 and up. No ads, no chat, no accounts, no in-app purchases and no personal data collected."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://dhl84.github.io/beakerwise/privacy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://dhl84.github.io/beakerwise/terms.html", "publisher_name": "David Lee", "support_website_url": "https://dhl84.github.io/beakerwise/support.html", 